-- title:
--   Tame vertex stabilisers for Γ₁ on the q' side
-- statement:
--   The statement is set up inside the Čerednik–Drinfel'd frame on the $q'$ side, and its conclusion is a tameness assertion about vertex stabilisers on the Bruhat–Tits tree.
--
--   **Numerical data.** Natural numbers $N$ (nonzero), $q$, $q'$ with $q$ and $q'$ prime, $N$ squarefree (`hN`), $q \nmid N$ (`hqN`), $q' \nmid N$ (`hq'N`), $q' \neq q$ (`hqq'`), and $5 \le q$, $5 \le q'$ (`hq5`, `hq'5`); a nonzero natural number $D$ with $2Nqq' \mid D$ (`hD`).
--
--   **The valuation ring.** A valuation subring $A_1$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $A_1.\mathrm{LiesOverPrime}\,q'$, i.e. $q'$ is a non-unit of $A_1$ (`hA₁`), together with the hypothesis `hiso₁` that the decomposition subgroup of $A_1$ over $\mathbb Q$ acts isometrically for the valuation of $A_1$; a height-one prime $v_1$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ with $q' \in v_1$ (`hv₁`). Throughout, $\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A_1$ denotes the closure of the prime subfield inside the completion $A_1.\mathrm{valuation.Completion}$.
--
--   **Definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_2, b_2$ with `hdef₂`: $a_2 < 0$, $b_2 < 0$, and for every finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_2, b_2] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies over $q$. Submodules $\Lambda_2, R_2$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_2, b_2]$ with $\Lambda_2$ a maximal order (`hΛ₂`: an order maximal among the orders containing it), $R_2$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (`hR₂`: an intersection of two maximal orders whose relative index in the first is $N$), and $R_2 \le \Lambda_2$ (`hRΛ₂`). A finite-idelic unit $n_2$ in $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\,R_2\,q'$ (`hn₂`), subject to: `hS₂`, that $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_2\,n_2 = R_2 \cap n_2 R_2 n_2^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nq'$; `hnorm₂`, that $n_2$ normalises this order; `hsq₂`, that the shift by $n_2$ on the class set of the finite-idelic stabiliser of $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_2\,n_2$ is an involution; finiteness of the two class sets involved; and `hlaws₂`, the predicate `ClassSetHeckeLaws N q' Λ₂ R₂ n₂`, namely that the edge Hecke matrices commute pairwise, the vertex Hecke matrices commute pairwise, for $\ell \neq q$ each of the two degeneracy maps intertwines edge with vertex Hecke operators, and the joint kernel of the degeneracy maps is stable under the edge Hecke operators.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion side and the curve.** Rationals $a, b$ with `hB`: $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a, b] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly at the places over $q$ and over $q'$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ in $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a, b]$ (`hΛ`). A field $\overline F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is a curve over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (principal divisors exist, residue fields of all places are finite over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $\Omega_{\overline F/\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ is free of rank one) and essentially of finite type.
--
--   **Moduli data over the $D$-integral base.** A scheme $X$ with a morphism $\pi_X$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{Localization.Away}\,(D : \mathbb Z)$, a point $\overline s$ of that base with values in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and an assignment $\mathrm{pt}$ sending a fake elliptic curve over a ring $S$ (an abelian scheme of relative dimension two with $\Lambda$-action, level-$N$ structure and the trace condition of `FakeEllipticCurve`) to a point of $X$ over the given base point; the hypotheses `pt_iso`, `pt_pullback`, `pt_surjective`, `pt_injective` are the four moduli clauses: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change along ring maps and pullback of curves, and surjectivity and injectivity (up to isomorphism) on geometric points over algebraically closed fields. A curve model $\mathfrak M$ of $\overline F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak M}$ from $\mathfrak M.C$ to the pullback of $\pi_X$ along $\overline s$ with $e_{\mathfrak M}$ followed by the second projection equal to $\mathfrak M.\mathrm{toBase}$ (`he𝔐`), and a homomorphism $\mathrm{gal}$ from $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to the semilinear automorphisms of $\overline F$.
--
--   **Hecke tower.** Tower data $\mathbb T$ of function fields indexed by the primes $\ell \notin \{q, q'\}$, Galois actions $\mathrm{galT}$ on each, and pairs of semilinear automorphisms $W$, $WT$; the hypothesis `tw` is the witness structure `ModuliTowerWitnessD` (its fields are summarised here): it attaches to every place of $\overline F$ a fake elliptic curve over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose moduli point is the corresponding point of $X$ under $e_{\mathfrak M}$, does the same with extra level $\ell$ for the places of each tower field, bijectively up to isomorphism, requires $\mathrm{gal}$ and $\mathrm{galT}$ to induce the given automorphism on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $W$, $WT$ to be $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-linear, and records the level-restriction and level-isogeny relations between the tower levels and the base.
--
--   **The $p$-adic matrix embedding.** An injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_1$ from $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_2, b_2]$ to $2 \times 2$ matrices over $\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A_1$ (`hι₁`), a homomorphism $\rho_1$ from $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_2, b_2]^{\times}$ to $\mathrm{PGL}_2(\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A_1)$ given by reducing $\iota_1$ projectively (`hρ₁`); a pseudo-uniformiser $\varpi_1$ whose image in the completion is $q'$ (`hϖ₁`), and the hypothesis `hdom₁` that the ring $\mathrm{HolRingOf}\,\varpi_1\,\rho_1$ of holomorphic functions on the $\varpi_1$-upper half plane is a domain.
--
--   **Hecke correspondence elements and the groups $\Gamma_1$.** Families $s_1$ and $sf_1$ indexed by the primes $\ell \notin \{q, q'\}$, of quaternion units and of finite-idelic units, with `hs₁`: at each place not over $q'$ the idele $sf_1(\ell)$ is the image of $s_1(\ell)$, at the places over $q'$ it is $1$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $sf_1(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}\,\Lambda_2\,(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_2\,n_2)\,\ell$ if $\ell \mid N$ and in $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\,(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_2\,n_2)\,\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_1(\ell)) = \ell$. A family $\Gamma_1$ of subgroups of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_2, b_2]^{\times}$ indexed by $\mathrm{Option}$ of those primes, with `hΓ₁0`: $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none})$ consists of the units $x$ lying in $\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R_2\,v_1$ — that is, whose image in $(\mathbb H \otimes \mathbb Q_w)^{\times}$ lies in the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_2$ at $w$, for every finite place $w \neq v_1$ — and such that $\mathrm{padicValRat}\,q'\,(\mathrm{nrd}\,x)$ is even; and `hΓ₁ℓ`: $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)$ is the intersection of $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none})$ with its conjugate by $s_1(\ell)$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner elements.** Families $w_1$, $\overline w_1$ with `hw₁`: $w_1(\mathrm{none})$ lies in $\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R_2\,v_1$ and has reduced norm $q'$, and for each $\ell$ the element $w_1(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)$ lies in $\mathrm{awayUnits}\,(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_2\,(sf_1\ \ell))\,v_1$ and has reduced norm $q'$; and `hwbar₁`, the corresponding conditions for $\overline w_1$: reduced norm $q$, membership in the local box units away from $v_1$ and away from $q$, and normalisation of the local boxes of $R_2$ (respectively of $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_2\,(sf_1\ \ell)$) and of $\Lambda_2$ at every place $u \neq v_1$.
--
--   **Decomposition group, character.** A homomorphism $d\mathrm{Iso}_1$ from the decomposition subgroup of $A_1$ to the isometric automorphisms of the completion, inducing the given action (`hdIso₁`); a homomorphism $\chi$ from the decomposition subgroup to $\mathbb Z/2$, trivial on inertia (`hχ₁`), nontrivial on every Frobenius at $q'$ (`hχ₂`), and trivial exactly on the elements fixing the $q'^2$-roots of unity, i.e. the elements of the residue field of $A_1$ with $x^{q'^2} = x$ (`hχ₃`).
--
--   **The coefficient rings.** A characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain $\mathcal O_0$ (`hdvr₀`) with irreducible $\pi$ (`hπ`), $\pi$-adically complete (`hcpl`), residue field of cardinality $q'$ (`hres`), $(q') = (\pi)$ (`hunr`), and $\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A_1$ as fraction field; a characteristic-zero $\mathcal O_0$-algebra domain $\mathrm{Onr}$ with an $\mathcal O_0$-automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to `hOc` (completeness), `hOm` (maximality of $(\pi)$), `hOa` (every element satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O_0$ modulo $\pi$), `hOcl` (every monic polynomial of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$) and `hFr` ($\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{q'}$ modulo $\pi$); a homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet}$ from $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A_1)$ to $\mathbb Z$ characterised by `hvdet` through the $\pi$-valuation of the determinant; a ring map $\psi_0$ from $\mathrm{Onr}$ to the completion with `hψ₀` (values in the unit ball) and `hψ₀𝒪` (compatibility over $\mathcal O_0$); $\pi = \varpi_1.\varpi$ (`hπϖ`), $N$ a unit in $\mathcal O_0$ (`hN₀`), `h𝒪₀` identifying the image of $\mathcal O_0$ with the unit ball of $\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A_1$, and `hrk`, a rank-one condition on the valuation.
--
--   **Integral models and degeneracies.** A scheme $\mathcal X_0$ with $f_0$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_0$ and moduli map $\mathrm{pt}_0$ such that `h𝒳₀`: $\mathcal X_0$ is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves of level $N$ over $\mathcal O_0$, with $\mathcal X_0$ integral and $f_0$ flat, separated, locally of finite type and quasi-compact; for each prime $\ell \notin \{q', q\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_0(\ell)$ with $g_0(\ell)$ and $\mathrm{ptT}_0(\ell)$ which is a coarse moduli space for the same objects with extra level $\ell$ (`h𝒴₀`); two degeneracy morphisms $d_{00}(\ell), d_{10}(\ell)$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) realising on moduli points the forgetting of the extra level (`hd₀`) and the quotient by it (`hd₁`); endomorphisms $\mathrm{ar}$ and $\overline{\mathrm{ar}}$ of $\mathcal X_0$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $q'$ and at $q$ respectively on moduli points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The uniformisation.** Maps $\Theta$ and $\Theta T(\ell)$ from the functor sending a $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O_0$-algebra $B$ to the pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O_0$-algebra map $\mathrm{Onr} \to B$ and a Deligne datum in $\Omega$, to the nilpotent points of $f_0$, respectively of $g_0(\ell)$. The hypothesis `hCD` is a conjunction of ten clauses: naturality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta T(\ell)$; invariance of $\Theta$ under the twisted action of the image under $\iota_1$ of $\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R_2\,v_1$, and of $\Theta T(\ell)$ under that of the intersection of $\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R_2\,v_1$ with its conjugate by $s_1$ at the corresponding prime; over every algebraically closed $\pi$-nilpotent field, surjectivity of $\Theta$ and $\Theta T(\ell)$ in the second variable and the statement that two Deligne data have the same image precisely when they are related by the twisted action of an element of the relevant group; the initiality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta T(\ell)$ among such invariant natural families; compatibility of $\Theta T(\ell)$ with $d_{00}(\ell)$ and, through the twisted action of $s_1$, with $d_{10}(\ell)$; and compatibility of $\Theta$ with $\mathrm{ar}$ via the Frobenius twist by $1$ and with $\overline{\mathrm{ar}}$ via the twisted action of $\overline w_1(\mathrm{none})$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of the above, two assertions hold, both about vertices of the lattice tree $\mathrm{LT.LatticeTree.Vertex}\,\mathcal O_0\,(\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A_1)$, that is, homothety classes of full $\mathcal O_0$-lattices in $(\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A_1)^2$.
--
--   First: for every vertex $v$, the cardinality ($\mathrm{Nat.card}$) of the set of $g \in \mathrm{PGL}_2(\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A_1)$ which lie in the image of $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none})$ under $\rho_1$ and satisfy $g \cdot v = v$, regarded as an element of $A_1.\mathrm{valuation.Completion}$, has valuation $1$.
--
--   Second: for every prime $i \notin \{q', q\}$ and every vertex $v$, the same holds for the stabiliser of $v$ in the image under $\rho_1$ of $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{some}\,i)$, the prime $i$ being read as an index away from $q$ and $q'$ by interchanging the two components of its defining conjunction: the cardinality of $\{g \in \mathrm{PGL}_2(\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A_1) : g \in \rho_1(\Gamma_1(\mathrm{some}\,i)),\ g \cdot v = v\}$, cast into the completion, has valuation $1$.
--
--   In particular each such stabiliser is finite (an infinite one would give $\mathrm{Nat.card} = 0$, of valuation $0$) and its order is a unit at the place of $A_1$, hence prime to $q'$.
--
--   This is the tameness input for the Čerednik–Drinfel'd side at $q'$: the stabilisers in $\mathrm{PGL}_2$ of vertices of the Bruhat–Tits tree under the $q'$-side arithmetic groups $\Gamma_1$, at the base level and at each extra level $\ell$, are finite of order invertible at the place under consideration, which is what makes the quotient of the formal upper half plane by these groups behave as in Mumford's construction. It is consumed by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_mumfordEmbedding_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_one_zero_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_mumfordEmbedding_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_one_zero_of_two_mul_dvd), whose frame of hypotheses it shares, and it rests on the finiteness and order estimate for such stabilisers recorded in [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.finite_stabilizer_vertex_and_not_dvd_natCard_of_mumfordSideFrame`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.finite_stabilizer_vertex_and_not_dvd_natCard_of_mumfordSideFrame).
